  "section_notes": "S1 is strict on reporting and customer notice with no phase-in. S2 sets a 5% limit at 55 °C with a 36-month transition but no numeric interim cap, and gives per-model results to customers and regulators but not the public. S3 requires remote shut-off on new units and a 6-year retrofit. S4 requires built-in suppression after 36 months. S5 uses an 8/100k assessment trigger but leaves recall to regulator discretion, with open-ended corrective alternatives and prompt notices."
